 "description": "COL-13 stage 2 of 2: the Color tab section for the stage-18/19 color\npackage the core commit wired. Section order mirrors the native stage\norder — the wheel + split block sits between the CFA toggles and\nSaturation (temp 16, tint 17, wheel 18, split 19, saturat 20) — so the\npanel reads like the pipeline it drives.\n\nThe wheel (ColorWheel.kt): one disc, three band tabs (Shadows /\nMidtones / Highlights, SingleChoiceSegmentedButtonRow; rememberSaveable\nUI-only state — the grade stores three independent band offsets, the\ntabs only choose which the drag edits). The disc's colors ARE the\nstage-18 gain math: ColorWheelMath.gainsAt evaluates the engine's\n2^0.5x / 2^0.5y / 2^-0.5x exponents; discColor maps them to display\nrange, max-normalized, mixed toward neutral gray by offset magnitude —\nthe classic radial-strength idiom, and the fix for the center: plain\nmax-normalization renders the gains-1 ",
